# Runtime data — user accounts, progress, reviews, audit logs.
# The dev DB is in server/data/, prod lives in a Docker named volume.
# `src/data/` is NOT ignored — that's the curated Kazakh card data
# (a1.json…c1.json) and the topic-name list (decks.json), both
# committed to the repo so a fresh clone has the full deck without
# needing to re-run the PDF parser.
server/data/

# Generated TTS audio — pre-generated at install time and committed
# to the repo so a fresh clone has audio for every Kazakh word in
# the official decks without needing to run the TTS pipeline.
# Per-word lazy generation for user-added cards (see
# scripts/tts_service.py + POST /api/tts/synthesize) lands in the
# same directory at runtime — those new files are NOT gitignored
# either, so a "wipe audio and rebuild" is `git checkout public/audio`
# followed by `docker compose --profile tools run --rm qazaq-tts`
# to regenerate anything missing.
# public/audio/

# Playwright e2e output (reports, traces, screenshots)
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/

# Throwaway screenshot scripts used during dev (named `_shot-*.mjs`)
_shot-*.mjs
_shot-*.png

# Local TTS model cache used by `scripts/generate-tts.py` and the
# Docker build. Downloaded on demand from HF, not part of the repo.
models/

# Misc
*.tsbuildinfo
.cache/
.vite/
coverage/
/data/

# Root-level data/ dir catches the stray sqlite file when the
# server is started without DB_PATH (the .gitignore'd
# server/data/ is for the real DB; data/ is for boot-time
# accidents that should never be committed).
